CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Permissive

Preamble

CERN has developed this licence to promote collaboration among hardware
designers and to provide a legal tool which supports the freedom to use,
study, modify, share and distribute hardware designs and products based on
those designs. Version 2 of the CERN Open Hardware Licence comes in three
variants: CERN-OHL-P (permissive); this licence, CERN-OHL-W (weakly
reciprocal) and CERN-OHL-S (strongly reciprocal).

The CERN-OHL-P is copyright CERN 2020. Anyone is welcome to use the
CERN-OHL-P, in unmodified form only.

Use of this Licence does not imply any endorsement by CERN of any Licensor
or their designs nor does it imply any involvement by CERN in their
development.

1 Definitions

1.1 'Licence' means this CERN-OHL-P.

1.2 'Compatible Licence' means any licence listed in the Compatible
Licences List published at https://ohwr.org/cernohl as may be amended from
time to time.

1.3 'Components' means parts, sub-assemblies, code, libraries, software,
firmware or data, intended to be incorporated into or used with the Source
or a Product. Components are not themselves the Source.

1.4 'Documentation' means information in the Source which is intended to
provide an explanation of and to inform on the use, function and assembly
of the design, and includes, without limitation, bills of material,
assembly instructions, test or verification procedures and information on
required Components and tools.

1.5 'Licensor' means a person or legal entity granting this Licence.

1.6 'Licensee' or 'You' means any person exercising rights under this
Licence.

1.7 'Made' or 'Make' means to have applied the Source to a process such
that a tangible Product (which includes everything from raw materials to
assembled and operating Products) is produced.

1.8 'Notice' means copyright, acknowledgement and trademark notices,
references to the location of any Notices, modification notices
(subsection 3.3 (b)) and all notices that refer to this Licence and to
the absence of warranties.

1.9 'Product' means any device, component, work, physical object or
service created as a result of using the Source.

1.10 'Source' means the version of the design preferred by a Licensor for
making modifications to it, and includes all the Documentation necessary
to Make the Product. The Licence covers Source which the Licensor has
chosen to make available, and does not impose any obligation to provide
additional Documentation.

2 Applicability

2.1 This Licence governs the use, copying, modification, communication
and distribution of the Source, and the Making of Products. By exercising
any right granted under this Licence, You irrevocably accept these terms
and conditions.

2.2 This Licence is granted by the Licensor directly to You, and shall
apply worldwide and without limitation in time.

2.3 You shall not attempt to restrict by contract or otherwise the rights
granted under this Licence to other Licensees.

2.4 This Licence is not intended to restrict fair use, fair dealing, or
any other similar right.

3 Copying, modifying and distributing the Source

3.1 You may copy and distribute verbatim copies of the Source, in any
medium, provided You retain all Notices.

3.2 You may modify copies of the Source, and distribute such modified
copies, provided that Your modified copies are clearly marked as such.

3.3 You may distribute copies of modified Source provided that You meet
the following conditions:
  a) the new Notices are placed in obvious positions in any medium where
     they are likely to be noticed by subsequent users;
  b) where You distribute or communicate any modified Source, You make
     available the Source to recipients;
  c) You do not place restrictions on the further exercise by any
     recipient of the rights granted under this Licence.

4 Making and distributing Products

4.1 You may Make Products and/or distribute them, provided that You
either provide each recipient with a copy of the Source or inform them
where the Source can be obtained.

4.2 Where You distribute or communicate a Product, You must include the
Notices in or with the Product.

5 Research and Development

The making available of Source by a Licensor, or the use of Source by
Licensees to develop, prototype, evaluate, research, simulate, modify or
test designs is not subject to the obligations in section 4.

